{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Appends a memory entry to a kb domain's memory facet: validated atomic append (entry.claim required), server-side timestamp, exact-claim dedupe, canonical serialization, journaled on the domain's _patches. Sources auto-stamp at write time - the staleness mechanism: a facet pointer ({lib,ctl,facet}) gets the referent's content hash; a repo file pointer ({repo,path} in a dev.git-registered repo) gets the working-tree content hash plus HEAD commit as provenance; a bare {doc} that resolves inside exactly ONE registered repo is upgraded to a checkable repo pointer. One-memory-cycle A1: a deposit aimed at a SHIPPED domain (data/<lib> tracked inside a registered repo) lands in the instance-local overlay (runtime/agent/memory-overlay/<lib>.<ctl>.jsonl, result carries routed:overlay) instead of the committed facet - recall reads the union immediately, promote is the only door to shipped bytes, and normal operation never dirties a tracked repo. Local libraries (kb, scratch, anything untracked) keep the in-place journaled write.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::system_call::system_call;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\n","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"domain","type":"String"},{"name":"entry","type":"JSONObject"},{"name":"author","type":"String"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"kkjzwq19fec41bc01j1","readers":[],"time":1787320370151,"username":"system","writers":[]}